      "problem": "Given that  $9-24r+16{r}^{2}=0$, find $r.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that the left-hand side is a perfect square. It just needs to be factored:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9-24r+16{r}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {3}^{2}-2\\cdot 3\\cdot 4r+(4r)^{2} & =0 \\\\ (3-4r)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(3-4r)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{0} \\\\ |3-4r| & =0 \\\\ 3-4r & =0 \\\\ 4r & =3 \\\\ r & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
